## Local findings so far
- The 3-minute warm phase generated 1,277,454 rows in each default-batch run, versus only 359,982 SoG rows in `sweep_control_fixed` and 368,502 in `querybel_30m`.
- Ring positions imply 235,484 warm rows remained in the control's final 595,466-row replay (39.5% live; about 19.8% of the configured mixed sampler). `sweep2_S6` retained 64.6% warm rows. Do not propose clearing all warm replay without qualification: `arch_j_30` did that and prediction spread collapsed from about 0.41 to 0.15.
- Fresh-row loss was consistently much larger than old-row loss. In the control's last five minutes: training 0.0293, old 0.0201, fresh 0.0358. This is distribution shift/noisy bootstrap, not the usual stale-row-underfit story.
- The configured value/policy objective ended near 0.029 + 0.05*1.84 = 0.121 total, so the weighted policy term was about 3.1x the value term by loss magnitude. New gradient telemetry must decide whether it also dominates shared-trunk gradients.
- The horizon payoff is estimated from only about 10 games per 10-second window: control cap value was zero in 67% of epochs and jumped across 0..0.15 with std 0.040. This makes sparse outcome grounding nonstationary.
- Search refinement is not the top lever: `sweep2_S6` made 148,713 versus 359,982 rows and scored 0.255 against the control over 200 games. More refined search lost 185 Elo.
- Zero-sum max residual reached 0.3-0.5, but older projection/penalty experiments lost strength. Added RMS telemetry before ranking this.
- Existing `batch_configs` was broken and always logged 6; instrumentation now records the actual config count.
- The instrumented run made 360,041 solves at 222.5/s and 359,065 rows. The final live replay was 39.9% warm, 29.6% play, and 30.5% query; the last five minutes sampled 21.1%, 39.5%, and 39.4% respectively.
- Last-five-minute value loss was 0.02966: old 0.01880 and fresh 0.03540. Outcome RMSE/MAE was 0.7870/0.6535, correlation 0.3585, and calibration slope 0.5732. Only 0.736% of sampled config targets were TD(1) outcomes.
- Last-five-minute target age was 748.5s mean and 1,482.3s p90. Main-line delivery delay was 69.0s mean and 95.7s p90 overall.
- Policy CE was 1.8635, target entropy 1.5747, and KL 0.2888. At weight 0.05, the reducible KL term was about 0.0144 versus value loss 0.0297. Gradient norm was 0.252 mean, 0.680 max, with no clipping. Zero-sum residual was 0.0296 RMS and 0.3528 max.
- The run completed 1,594 games with 12.0% horizon hits. Horizon shaping had annealed to zero throughout the last five minutes. Final beat the 15-minute snapshot 31-9 and Greedy 40-0 in the 40-game ladder.
- A prior matched 200-game ablation measured `p_td1=0.2` over `0.0` at 111-89, +38.2 Elo. Removing queries lost 34.7 Elo; publishing every 0.2 rather than 1 minute lost 20.8 Elo; stronger search lost 185 Elo.

